  "reason": "The current best (config_039, acc=0.7250) uses transformer aggregation with scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + weighted fusion. We have only tested transformer aggregation so far; the effect of aggregation method is an important untested design axis. config_004 is a clean ablation: it holds all other settings at their best-known values (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, weighted fusion) and swaps transformer for avgpool. This directly tests whether the more complex transformer aggregation is contributing meaningfully or whether a simpler pooling suffices. Under a 6-experiment remaining budget, resolving this architectural question is high-value: if avgpool matches transformer, it confirms a simpler direction to exploit; if it lags, it validates transformer and narrows the search space, freeing later experiments to focus on image encoder or profile setting."
}

